Consider the given two statements:
<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1" style="width:500px;"><tbody><tr><td><strong>I:</strong></td><td>The most widely used compound as source of ethylene is ethephon.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>II:</strong></td><td>Ethephon in an aqueous solution is readily absorbed and transported within the plant and releases ethylene slowly.</td></tr></tbody></table>
&nbsp;

<table border="1" cellpadding="1" cellspacing="1"><tbody><tr><td>1.</td><td>Both<strong> I</strong> and<strong> II </strong>are correct and<strong> II </strong>explains <strong>I</strong></td></tr><tr><td>2.</td><td>Both<strong> I </strong>and<strong> II</strong> are correct but <strong>II</strong> does not explain <strong>I</strong></td></tr><tr><td>3.</td><td><strong>I</strong> is correct but <strong>II </strong>is incorrect</td></tr><tr><td>4.</td><td><strong>I</strong> is incorrect but <strong>II</strong> is correct</td></tr></tbody></table>&nbsp;

